      "writtenOn": "2013-07-19T01:09:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are going to want to put some guarding in here to prevent invalid data being passed and probably raise out bad request instead of an exception and a straight ISE.\n\nOne example case is that request.GET is a dict, and dict.get() returns a NoneType as default, so if oauth_consumer_key doesn\u0027t exist you get None back on the .get().  Split cannot be called on NoneType and you end up with an ISE instead of a more useful error.\n\nThere should also be tests for BadRequests/invalid requests being sent through.",
      "revId": "54c9c30b9b5cb747387af02b46e79aa44920e2aa",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
